{
  "$comment": [
    "Prototype of a declarative text-effect registry (registry v2) for docs/text-motion-references.md.",
    "Every effect is data, not code: per-channel keyframe tracks over the effect's local time u in [0,1].",
    "The SAME file is interpreted by two engines: text_motion_stack.py (Python -> libass/ASS for the MP4)",
    "and the JavaScript twin in docs/mockups/text-effects-stack.html (live preview). That is what keeps",
    "preview and render identical and what makes effects stackable: channels are composed, not overwritten.",
    "",
    "phase    in | hold | out           (lane in the GUI: Enter / While shown / Exit)",
    "unit     char | word | line | text (what one animated 'piece' is; users may override per layer)",
    "duration seconds per unit (in/out) or loop period (hold)",
    "stagger  seconds between units (in/out) or phase offset between units (hold)",
    "order    forward | reverse | center | edges | random",
    "loop     hold only: loop | pingpong | once (once = stretched over the whole text window)",
    "tracks   channel -> [[u, value, easing?], ...] or a generator {sine|noise|flicker|path}",
    "         values: number | '#rrggbb' | 'base' (colour below this layer) | {'rand':[a,b]} per unit",
    "channels opacity, scale, sx, sy, fill (multiply) | x, y, blur, spacing, line (em, add) |",
    "         rz, rx, ry (degrees, add) | skew (shear, add) | glow, depth, rgb, orbit (max) |",
    "         colour (folded in stack order) | clip [l,t,r,b] of the unit box (intersected, only while the effect runs)",
    "copies   extra drawn copies: glow | trail | extrude | mirror | rgb | shadow | box",
    "content  at most ONE per phase: scramble | flap | count | countdown  (exclusive channel)",
    "caret    typewriter caret that follows the last visible letter"
  ],
